WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.787
Continuous monitoring isn't a
claim that monitoring happens.

2
00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:06.750
It's evidence an assessor
can check, and run again.

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:11.100
The practical test is simple: show me
an alert from the last thirty days,

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.025
the incident it opened
and what you did about it.

5
00:00:14.025 --> 00:00:17.908
So every incident keeps four
parts: the alert, the ticket,

6
00:00:17.908 --> 00:00:21.200
the response notes, and
a closure with its proof.

7
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.588
Closing a finding takes three steps.

8
00:00:23.588 --> 00:00:25.399
The platform owner fixes it.

9
00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:27.712
The next scan or check shows it's gone.

10
00:00:27.712 --> 00:00:29.387
And the record links the two.

11
00:00:29.387 --> 00:00:34.775
The decision: a finding closes only on
that re-test, never on a ticket status.

12
00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:38.020
Next, how you know the
monitoring itself is working.
